.TH QXCTL-NASDAQ 1 "March 2026" "QuanuX System" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qxctl-nasdaq \- Manage the QuanuX NASDAQ ITCH/OUCH Adapter boundaries.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qxctl nasdaq
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B qxctl-nasdaq
toolset commands manage the live-cutover constraints, preload directory status, and sequence recovery matrix of the QuanuX-Omega NASDAQ adapter. 
It interfaces physically with the `StockDirectoryRegistry` singleton limits natively.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Returns the active `RegistryReadiness` bound (ColdStart, Ready, Degraded, etc.).
.TP
.B recover <SEQUENCE_TARGET>
Physically transitions the node into `RecoverySync` actively searching for the specified target catchup limit securely.
.TP
.B override
Applies an `OperatorOverride` degradation lock natively stopping all automated sequential logic implicitly. Requires manual `qxctl nasdaq clear` to restore trading flows naturally.
.TP
.B clear
Unlocks an operator override manually restoring execution streams functionally cleanly cleanly functionally statically perfectly safely nicely flexibly securely smoothly.
